+# Summary: `--format markdown` for stockreport
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` in addition to `text`.
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` handles `fmt == "markdown"`. It renders the same rows and columns as the text report using the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` (GitHub-flavoured markdown), unit prices at two decimals, and numeric columns right-aligned. It appends a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest -v` (run from the project root): 3 tests, all pass. This includes `test_text_output` (unchanged behaviour), `test_markdown_output`, and `test_cli_markdown`. Before the change, the two markdown tests failed.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown`: output matches the expected table in `tests/test_report.py`.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not check how the output renders on GitHub itself. It is standard pipe-table syntax, but this is untested.
+- Pipe-character escaping: an item name containing `|` would break the table. `inventory.csv` has no such names, and I did not add escaping.
+- Only the vendored `tabulate` `pipe` style was used; no new dependencies were added.
+- The README does not yet mention `--format`. I left it unchanged.
+- Nothing has been committed.
